- crates/eng-platform-gcmouse: a Cargo.toml like the other skeletons, with
  no dependencies. objc2-game-controller needs G3 first; T14 adds it under
  `[target.'cfg(target_os = "macos")'.dependencies]`.
- src/lib.rs: a doc comment (spec 6.10, decision 11, task T14), then
  `#![forbid(clippy::undocumented_unsafe_blocks)]` (ADR-0021: an `unsafe`
  block without a `// SAFETY:` comment fails clippy), then `mod macos`
  behind `#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]`, so the crate is empty on every
  other target. src/macos.rs holds a doc comment only.
- Unlike every other crate's root, this one does not forbid `unsafe_code`.
  T14 allows it in one module file (ADR-0021), and a `forbid` at the root
  would refuse that `allow`. The workspace lint still denies it, so the
  crate compiles no `unsafe` today. The crate is not core, so arch-check
  requires no root attribute.
- architecture.toml:
  - `[crates.eng-platform-gcmouse]`, `layer = "L1"`, before
    eng-platform-winit, which gains it in its `same_layer`;
  - `[floor]` gains `objc2-game-controller = "eng-platform-gcmouse"` and
    `eng-platform-gcmouse = "eng-platform-winit"`, and its comment now
    says "crates with one user" (ADR-0021). Layering alone lets any higher
    crate depend on an L1 crate, and cargo-deny's wrapper ban runs only in
    CI's lint job; arch-check runs in `quick`. Its floor rule looks up
    every normal dependency by name, workspace crates included
    (`xtask/src/arch.rs:198-204`), so no xtask change. Dev and build
    dependencies are not checked, as for every floor crate.
- Cargo.toml: its `[workspace.dependencies]` path. Cargo.lock gains the
  path package and nothing else.
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "Layers": the winit line gains the edge, and the
  floor-rule sentence is rewritten to name all three users.

